            <ArticleTitle>Mycotic aneurysm of the left anterior descending coronary artery after coronary artery bypass graft surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1601-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2010.11.018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mycotic aneurysms of the coronary artery are extremely uncommon and can be very difficult to diagnose. We report a unique case of a mycotic aneurysm of the left anterior descending coronary artery with a history of two-vessel off-pump coronary artery bypass graft surgery 9 months previously. The aneurysmectomy was successful.</AbstractText>
